Environment: Windows amd64, Go 1.27.3, GOEXPERIMENT=greenteagc,jsonv2, GOMAXPROCS=4.
Working directory: backend.
USAGE_EXPORT_TEST_DSN points only to the isolated local PostgreSQL test service on 127.0.0.1:55435.

Initial lifecycle unit / database run:
go test -p 2 ./internal/service ./internal/repository -run 'TestUsageExport' -count=1 -v
Log: xlsx-lifecycle-unit.log
Result: service and repository passed, including database lease, quota, deletion, ticket, owner filtering and keyset index tests.

First lifecycle race run:
go test -race -p 2 ./internal/service ./internal/repository -run 'TestUsageExport' -count=1 -v
Log: xlsx-lifecycle-race.log
Result: service passed. Repository database checks encountered repeated local PostgreSQL TCP connection closures while WSL was unavailable; retained the complete original failure output.

Changes added after the initial runs require the final integrated rerun:
- Independent artifact worker lease, including orphan-owner cleanup and cluster execution capacity.
- Download file lease, close-before-release, cancellation, failed renewal and deadline checks.
- Exact raw model cursor captured before display normalization.
- Authorization before the download file transaction to avoid connection-pool nesting.

Final verification is run serially by the coordinating task using the same TestUsageExport command and isolated database.
